 "about": "Field classes of the appliances_cooking domain's types for the house ledger (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.3, lint L-WATCH; WP-D appliances_cooking). 'fields' classifies every property name of house_sim/data/types/appliances_cooking.json and the fields this domain's verbs, hooks and systems write onto its own types, for the types that file defines; a dotted name is one sub-key of a dict field, '<head>.*' its other sub-keys. Ratings, sizes, kinds and capabilities are identity; knobs, programs, lit burners, locks and a delayed start are settings; what a heater, a thermostat or a program drives (temperatures, countdowns, status lights, preheated, load_state, ringing, alarms, a pressure cooker's pressure, an espresso boiler, a delayed start counting down) is process; damage a heater or program does (a scratched coating, a warped or discoloured part, an overheated motor, a scorched or melted handle, milk dried on a steam wand, a dead igniter, a dislodged burner cap) is a condition with its worse direction; fuel and doses used up (charcoal, propane, an espresso dose) are content; ash and toaster crumbs are mess loads (guard mess). 'types' refines one type: a toaster's fill_level follows the slices in its slots and its allergen contamination is its normal use, a microwave's settings.time_s is the countdown it shows, a dishwasher filter's or sump's soil is the food it is there to catch, an electric griddle's grease trough is a mess load, the program a dishwasher, an oven, a toaster or a cooker runs is the copy of its panel setting (bookkeeping: the setting is watched), a dishwasher's detergent cup lid opens by the program; generic_item lists the names this domain writes onto the core generic_item that stands in for pots, pans, dishes and food (damage a dishwasher does to an unsuitable item, a handle direction on a burner, a dish on the oven floor) and that the kernel's watch_fields.json does not classify. water_sensitive: types a soaking spoils whose record does not say water_safe false (paper filters, charcoal, detergent pods and powder, coffee pods, oven mitts and pot holders that then conduct heat, digital timers and probe thermometers); every countertop appliance is water_safe false already.",
